{{Term/Store|Barrel|Barrels|Series, MM, MM3D, TWW, TP, SS, SSHD, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Object]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite Guide|MM Nintendo|page=80}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Ocean, #5: Barrel|Vision|MM3D}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Guide|TWW Nintendo|page=8}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= E |publisher= |page= 273 {{Exp Game|TMC}}}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Guide|TP Prima|page= 132}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Good morning, Link! Today's the big {{Color SSHD|Red|Wing Ceremony}}, right? I wanted to fly too, but I... I didn't make the cut, so I'm stuck back here at the academy. Plus, I've got to move these {{Color SSHD|Red|barrels}} over to the kitchen.|Fledge|SSHD}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Barrel|Game Screen|TotK}}</ref>{{Name Ref|TWWHD, TPHD, PH, ST, BotW}} Barrels go unnamed in {{OoS}} and {{CoH}}. Like [[Pot]]s, they usually reveal pickups such as [[Rupee]]s, [[Heart]]s, [[Arrow]]s, and [[Bomb]]s when broken. Depending on the game, Barrels may also have particular purposes or roles.

==Location and Uses==
==={{MM|-}}===
Barrels make their debut in {{MM}}, where they appear exclusively within the [[Pirates' Fortress]] and the [[Great Bay Temple]]. Appearing as large kegs, Barrels in {{MM|-}} cannot be lifted, although they can be broken with Bombs, by rolling into them, or by punching them in [[Goron Link|Goron form]]. A [[Stray Fairy]] in the Great Bay Temple can be found inside a Barrel. Barrels, being made of wood, can also be latched onto with the [[Hookshot]].

==={{OoS|-}}===
Barrels are used by the [[Hylian Knight]]s while they disguise themselves as a troupe of musicians to protect [[Din (Oracle)|Din]]. These Barrels are destroyed by [[Onox]] when he kidnaps the Oracle of Seasons.

==={{TWW|-}}===
